<DocsLayout title="Native Sidecars">
  <h1>Native Sidecars</h1>
  <p>Full content coming in SITE2 — this page will import <code>docs/plan/native_sidecar_plan.md</code>.</p>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Native sidecars are package-managed native binaries loaded by the Eta runtime
    through a versioned ABI (<code>eta-native-v1</code>). They extend the primitive
    environment with C++-backed functionality — torch tensors, nng messaging,
    Eigen stats — without hard-linking those libraries into core tools.
  </p>

  <h2>Key properties</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Declared in <code>eta.toml</code> under <code>[native]</code></li>
    <li>Selected by target triple at resolve time</li>
    <li>SHA-256 verified at materialization and load</li>
    <li>Loaded in deterministic lockfile order</li>
    <li>Extension hash embedded in <code>.etac</code> freshness metadata</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Stdlib sidecars</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>eta-log-sidecar</code> — spdlog-backed logging</li>
    <li><code>eta-stats-sidecar</code> — Eigen statistics</li>
    <li><code>eta-nng-sidecar</code> — nanomsg-next-gen messaging</li>
    <li><code>eta-torch-sidecar</code> — LibTorch tensors and autograd</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>

